msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:401
msgid "Dump information about this system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:403
msgid ""
"Dump a wide range of information about the current system.  If run from the "
"top of a binary tree for a CMake project it will dump additional information "
"such as the cache, log files etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:411
msgid "Print CMake config directory for user-wide FileAPI queries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:413
msgid "See :envvar:`CMAKE_CONFIG_DIR` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:419
msgid "Set the log ``<level>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:421
msgid ""
"The :command:`message` command will only output messages of the specified "
"log level or higher.  The valid log levels are ``ERROR``, ``WARNING``, "
"``NOTICE``, ``STATUS`` (default), ``VERBOSE``, ``DEBUG``, or ``TRACE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:425
msgid ""
"To make a log level persist between CMake runs, set :variable:"
"`CMAKE_MESSAGE_LOG_LEVEL` as a cache variable instead. If both the command "
"line option and the variable are given, the command line option takes "
"precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:430
msgid ""
"For backward compatibility reasons, ``--loglevel`` is also accepted as a "
"synonym for this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:433
msgid ""
"See the :command:`cmake_language(GET_MESSAGE_LOG_LEVEL)` command for a way "
"to query the current message logging level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:439
msgid ""
"Enable the :command:`message` command outputting context attached to each "
"message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:442
msgid ""
"This option turns on showing context for the current CMake run only. To make "
"showing the context persistent for all subsequent CMake runs, set :variable:"
"`CMAKE_MESSAGE_CONTEXT_SHOW` as a cache variable instead. When this command "
"line option is given, :variable:`CMAKE_MESSAGE_CONTEXT_SHOW` is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:452
msgid ""
"Enable logging of diagnostic messages produced by CMake in the SARIF format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:454
msgid ""
"Write diagnostic messages to a SARIF file at the path specified. Projects "
"can also set :variable:`CMAKE_EXPORT_SARIF` to ``ON`` to enable this feature "
"for a build tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:460
msgid ""
"Do not delete the files and directories created for :command:"
"`try_compile` / :command:`try_run` calls. This is useful in debugging failed "
"checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:464
msgid ""
"Note that some uses of :command:`try_compile` may use the same build tree, "
"which will limit the usefulness of this option if a project executes more "
"than one :command:`try_compile`.  For example, such uses may change results "
"as artifacts from a previous try-compile may cause a different test to "
"either pass or fail incorrectly.  This option is best used only when "
"debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:470
msgid ""
"(With respect to the preceding, the :command:`try_run` command is "
"effectively a :command:`try_compile`.  Any combination of the two is subject "
"to the potential issues described.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:476
msgid ""
"When this option is enabled, every try-compile check prints a log message "
"reporting the directory in which the check is performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:481
msgid "Put cmake in a debug mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:483
msgid ""
"Print extra information during the cmake run like stack traces with :command:"
"`message(SEND_ERROR)` calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:490
msgid "Put cmake find commands in a debug mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:492
msgid ""
"Print extra find call information during the cmake run to standard error. "
"Output is designed for human consumption and not for parsing. See also the :"
"variable:`CMAKE_FIND_DEBUG_MODE` variable for debugging a more local part of "
"the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:501
msgid ""
"Put cmake find commands in a debug mode when running under calls to :command:"
"`find_package(\\<pkg\\>) <find_package>`, where ``<pkg>`` is an entry in the "
"given comma-separated list of case-sensitive package names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:506
msgid ""
"Like :cmake-option:`--debug-find`, but limiting scope to the specified "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:513
msgid ""
"Put cmake find commands in a debug mode when called with ``<var>`` as the "
"result variable, where ``<var>`` is an entry in the given comma-separated "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:517
msgid ""
"Like :cmake-option:`--debug-find`, but limiting scope to the specified "
"variable names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:522 ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:528
msgid "Put cmake in trace mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:524
msgid "Print a trace of all calls made and from where."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:530
msgid "Like :cmake-option:`--trace`, but with variables expanded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:536
msgid "Put cmake in trace mode and sets the trace output format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:538
msgid "``<format>`` can be one of the following values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:540
msgid "``human``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:541
msgid ""
"Prints each trace line in a human-readable format. This is the default "
"format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:544
msgid "``json-v1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:545
msgid ""
"Prints each line as a separate JSON document. Each document is separated by "
"a newline (``\\n``). It is guaranteed that no newline characters will be "
"present inside a JSON document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:549
msgid "JSON trace format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:549
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"file\": \"/full/path/to/the/CMake/file.txt\",\n"
"  \"line\": 0,\n"
"  \"cmd\": \"add_executable\",\n"
"  \"args\": [\"foo\", \"bar\"],\n"
"  \"time\": 1579512535.9687231,\n"
"  \"frame\": 2,\n"
"  \"global_frame\": 4\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:562 ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:613
#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:786
msgid "The members are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:564
msgid "``file``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:565
msgid "The full path to the CMake source file where the function was called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:568
msgid "``line``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:569
msgid "The line in ``file`` where the function call begins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:571
msgid "``line_end``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:572
msgid ""
"If the function call spans multiple lines, this field will be set to the "
"line where the function call ends. If the function calls spans a single "
"line, this field will be unset. This field was added in minor version 2 of "
"the ``json-v1`` format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:577
msgid "``defer``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:578
msgid ""
"Optional member that is present when the function call was deferred by :"
"command:`cmake_language(DEFER)`.  If present, its value is a string "
"containing the deferred call ``<id>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:582
msgid "``cmd``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:583
msgid "The name of the function that was called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:585
msgid "``args``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:586
msgid "A string list of all function parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:588
msgid "``time``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:589
msgid "Timestamp (seconds since epoch) of the function call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:591
msgid "``frame``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:592
msgid ""
"Stack frame depth of the function that was called, within the context of "
"the  ``CMakeLists.txt`` being processed currently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:595
msgid "``global_frame``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:596
msgid ""
"Stack frame depth of the function that was called, tracked globally across "
"all ``CMakeLists.txt`` files involved in the trace. This field was added in "
"minor version 2 of the ``json-v1`` format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:600
msgid ""
"Additionally, the first JSON document outputted contains the ``version`` key "
"for the current major and minor version of the"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:603
msgid "JSON version format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:603
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"version\": {\n"
"    \"major\": 1,\n"
"    \"minor\": 2\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:615 ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:1199
#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:1247
msgid "``version``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:616
msgid ""
"Indicates the version of the JSON format. The version has a major and minor "
"components following semantic version conventions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:621
msgid "Put cmake in trace mode, but output only lines of a specified file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:623
msgid "Multiple options are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:627
msgid ""
"Put cmake in trace mode and redirect trace output to a file instead of "
"stderr."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:633
msgid "Compatibility synonym for ``-Wuninitialized``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:639
msgid ""
"Does nothing.  In CMake versions 3.2 and below this enabled warnings about "
"unused variables.  In CMake versions 3.3 through 3.18 the option was broken. "
"In CMake 3.19 and above the option has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:647
msgid "Compatibility synonym for ``-Wno-unused-cli``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:651
msgid "Find problems with variable usage in system files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:653
msgid ""
"Normally, unused and uninitialized variables are searched for only in :"
"variable:`CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR` and :variable:`CMAKE_BINARY_DIR`. This flag "
"tells CMake to warn about other files as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:661
msgid ""
"Ignore target property :prop_tgt:`COMPILE_WARNING_AS_ERROR` and variable :"
"variable:`CMAKE_COMPILE_WARNING_AS_ERROR`, preventing warnings from being "
"treated as errors on compile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:669
msgid ""
"Ignore target property :prop_tgt:`LINK_WARNING_AS_ERROR` and variable :"
"variable:`CMAKE_LINK_WARNING_AS_ERROR`, preventing warnings from being "
"treated as errors on link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:677
msgid ""
"Used in conjunction with :cmake-option:`--profiling-format` to output to a "
"given path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:682
msgid ""
"Enable the output of profiling data of CMake script in the given format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:684
msgid ""
"This can aid performance analysis of CMake scripts executed. Third party "
"applications should be used to process the output into human readable format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:687
msgid ""
"Currently supported values are: ``google-trace`` Outputs in Google Trace "
"Format, which can be parsed by the about:tracing tab of Google Chrome or "
"using a plugin for a tool like Trace Compass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:694
msgid ""
"Reads a :manual:`preset <cmake-presets(7)>` from CMake presets files. "
"``CMakePresets.json`` and ``CMakeUserPresets.json`` are the default files, "
"which must be located in the same directory as the top level ``CMakeLists."
"txt`` file.  A file can also be specified with :cmake-option:`--presets-"
"file`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:700
msgid ""
"The preset may specify the generator, the build directory, a list of "
"variables, and other arguments to pass to CMake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:703
msgid ""
"The :manual:`CMake GUI <cmake-gui(1)>` also recognizes and supports "
"``CMakePresets.json`` and ``CMakeUserPresets.json`` files. For full details "
"on these files, see :manual:`cmake-presets(7)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:707
msgid ""
"The presets are read before all other command line options, although the :"
"cmake-option:`-S` option can be used to specify the source directory "
"containing the ``CMakePresets.json`` and ``CMakeUserPresets.json`` files. If "
"neither :cmake-option:`-S` nor :cmake-option:`--presets-file` are given, the "
"current working directory is assumed to be the top level source directory "
"and must contain ``CMakePresets.json`` and/or ``CMakeUserPresets.json``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:714
msgid ""
"The options specified by the chosen preset (variables, generator, etc.) can "
"all be overridden by manually specifying them on the command line. For "
"example, if the preset sets a variable called ``MYVAR`` to ``1``, but the "
"user sets it to ``2`` with a :cmake-option:`-D` argument, the value ``2`` is "
"preferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:720
msgid ""
"The :cmake-option:`-B` option may optionally be specified with a different "
"binary directory than the one specified by the :preset:`configurePresets."
"binaryDir` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:725
msgid ""
"If :cmake-option:`--presets-file` is specified, neither of ``CMakePresets."
"json`` nor ``CMakeUserPresets.json`` are required to be present.  In prior "
"versions, the presence of these files in the top-level source directory "
"(whether via :cmake-option:`-S` or the current working directory) was "
"strictly required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:736 ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:858
#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:2007
msgid ""
"Reads :manual:`presets <cmake-presets(7)>` from the given ``<file>``. The "
"specified path may be absolute or relative to the current working directory. "
"If ``--presets-file`` is given, presets defined in ``CMakePresets.json`` and "
"``CMakeUserPresets.json`` will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:743
msgid ""
"Lists presets according to the specified ``<type>``.  Valid values are "
"``configure``, ``build``, ``test``, ``package``, ``workflow``, ``all``, or "
"any of those values with ``-defined`` appended.  The ``defined`` value is an "
"alias for ``configure-defined``.  If ``<type>`` is omitted, ``configure`` is "
"assumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:749
msgid ""
"The values without the ``-defined`` suffix list available presets.  The "
"suffixed values list all non-hidden defined presets of the selected type, "
"including unavailable presets with the reason they cannot be used.  The "
"``all`` and ``all-defined`` values select every preset type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:754
msgid ""
"If :cmake-option:`--presets-file` is specified, the presets defined in the "
"given ``<file>`` will be listed.  Otherwise, the top-level source directory "
"(whether via :cmake-option:`-S` or the current working directory) must "
"contain ``CMakePresets.json`` and/or ``CMakeUserPresets.json``. In prior "
"versions, the latter was strictly required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:761
msgid "Support for the ``workflow``, ``defined``, and ``-defined`` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:766
msgid ""
"Enables interactive debugging of the CMake language. CMake exposes a "
"debugging interface on the pipe named by :cmake-option:`--debugger-pipe` "
"that conforms to the `Debug Adapter Protocol`_ specification with the "
"following modifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:771
msgid ""
"The ``initialize`` response includes an additional field named "
"``cmakeVersion`` which specifies the version of CMake being debugged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:774
msgid "Debugger initialize response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:774
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"cmakeVersion\": {\n"
"    \"major\": 3,\n"
"    \"minor\": 27,\n"
"    \"patch\": 0,\n"
"    \"full\": \"3.27.0\"\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:788 ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:1204
msgid "``major``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:789
msgid "An integer specifying the major version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:791 ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:1206
msgid "``minor``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:792
msgid "An integer specifying the minor version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:794 ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:1208
msgid "``patch``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:795
msgid "An integer specifying the patch version number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:797
msgid "``full``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:798
msgid "A string specifying the full CMake version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:804
msgid ""
"Name of the pipe (on Windows) or domain socket (on Unix) to use for debugger "
"communication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:809
msgid "Logs all debugger communication to the specified file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:814
msgid "Build a Project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:818
msgid ""
"CMake provides a command-line signature to build an already-generated "
"project binary tree:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:821
msgid ""
"cmake --build <dir>                     [<options>] [-- <build-tool-"
"options>]\n"
"cmake --build [<dir>] --preset <preset> [<options>] [-- <build-tool-options>]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:826
msgid ""
"This abstracts a native build tool's command-line interface with the "
"following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:831
msgid ""
"Project binary directory to be built.  This is required (unless a preset is "
"specified) and must be first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:838
msgid ""
"Use a build :manual:`preset <cmake-presets(7)>` to specify build options. "
"The project binary directory is inferred from the :preset:`buildPresets."
"configurePreset` key unless a directory is specified after ``--build``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:843
msgid ""
"``cmake --build`` now supports specifying a build directory and preset "
"together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:847
msgid ""
"``cmake --build <dir> --preset`` no longer needs to be called from the "
"directory containing ``CMakePresets.json`` or ``CMakeUserPresets.json``. If :"
"cmake-build-option:`--presets-file` is specified, CMake will use that file; "
"otherwise, the presets file(s) can be inferred from the current build "
"directory's ``CMakeCache.txt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:865
msgid ""
"Lists the available build presets. With ``defined``, all non-hidden defined "
"build presets are listed, including unavailable presets with the reason they "
"cannot be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:869
msgid ""
"``cmake --build <dir> --list-presets`` no longer needs to be called from the "
"directory containing ``CMakePresets.json`` or ``CMakeUserPresets.json``. If :"
"cmake-build-option:`--presets-file` is specified, only presets defined in "
"the given ``<file>`` will be listed; otherwise, the presets file(s) are "
"inferred from the current build directory's ``CMakeCache.txt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:876 ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:2025
msgid "Support for the ``defined`` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:883
msgid ""
"The maximum number of concurrent processes to use when building. If "
"``<jobs>`` is omitted the native build tool's default number is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:886
msgid ""
"The :envvar:`CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL` environment variable, if set, "
"specifies a default parallel level when this option is not given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:889
msgid ""
"Some native build tools always build in parallel.  The use of ``<jobs>`` "
"value of ``1`` can be used to limit to a single job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:892
msgid ""
"When CMake is the one passing the parallel flag to the build tool (through "
"this option or the :envvar:`CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL` environment "
"variable) and that tool is GNU Make 4.0 or newer, the output of each recipe "
"is grouped so that concurrent jobs do not interleave.  Request parallelism "
"natively, e.g. ``cmake --build . -- -j``, to opt out and stream output as it "
"is produced.  Since :envvar:`CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL` likewise enables "
"grouping, unset it to opt out when it is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:904
msgid ""
"Build ``<tgt>`` instead of the default target.  Multiple targets may be "
"given, separated by spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:909
msgid "For multi-configuration tools, choose configuration ``<cfg>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:913
msgid ""
"Build target ``clean`` first, then build. (To clean only, use :option:`--"
"target clean <cmake--build --target>`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:920
msgid ""
"Resolve remote package references from external package managers (e.g. "
"NuGet) before build. When ``<value>`` is set to ``on`` (default), packages "
"will be restored before building a target.  When ``<value>`` is set to "
"``only``, the packages will be restored, but no build will be performed.  "
"When ``<value>`` is set to ``off``, no packages will be restored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:926
msgid ""
"If the target does not define any package references, this option does "
"nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:928
msgid ""
"This setting can be specified in a build preset (using "
"``resolvePackageReferences``). The preset setting will be ignored, if this "
"command line option is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:932
msgid ""
"If no command line parameter or preset option are provided, an environment- "
"specific cache variable will be evaluated to decide, if package restoration "
"should be performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/cmake.1.rst:936
msgid ""
"When using :ref:`Visual Studio Generators`, package references are defined "
"using the :prop_tgt:`VS_PACKAGE_REFERENCES` property. Package references are "
"restored using NuGet. It can be disabled by setting the "
"``CMAKE_VS_NUGET_PACKAGE_RESTORE`` variable to ``OFF``."
msgstr ""

